We propose \textbf{UP-VLA}, a unified understanding and prediction model for embodied agents. A single LLM backbone is trained with (1) a multi-modal understanding (MMU) objective on large-scale image-text data and (2) a future visual prediction (PRE) objective on robot video and action data. The two are fused by unified prompting and attention masking, and actions are generated conditioned on both a semantic scene description and predicted future image tokens. Our contributions are:
\begin{itemize}
\item UP-VLA, a VLA that jointly trains multi-modal understanding and future prediction in one autoregressive framework (\cref{sec:method}).
\item A unified prompting and attention-masking strategy that mixes continuous MMU tokens and discrete predictive tokens in a single LLM.
\item A joint prediction-and-understanding action mechanism that conditions actions on scene descriptions and predicted futures.
\item State-of-the-art results on CALVIN (ABC$\rightarrow$D average length 4.08, +33\% over GR-1) and real-world gains in both semantic generalization and precision tasks, with ablations isolating each component (\cref{sec:exp}).
\end{itemize}

