\paragraph{Simulation results.} \Cref{table1} shows that on ABC$\rightarrow$D UP-VLA completes 4.08 tasks in a row on average, versus 3.06 for GR-1 (about 33\% higher), 3.35 for 3D Diffuser Actor, 2.47 for RoboFlamingo and 1.44 for UP-VLA-RT-2. The gain holds at every chain length, notably 0.699 success on the fifth task versus 0.401 for GR-1. UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu (3.13) is close to GR-1, so the improvement comes from adding understanding rather than from the backbone alone. \Cref{table2} shows the same ordering on ABCD$\rightarrow$D: 4.42 against 4.21 for GR-1 and 4.09 for RoboFlamingo, a smaller gap, as expected when the test scene is seen in training.

