\paragraph{Visualization.} \Cref{fig:vis} shows VQA outputs and predicted future images. UP-VLA identifies objects and approximate relative positions, which supports action grounding, with occasional misidentification. Reading the two together: the VQA outputs show that understanding survives action fine-tuning, which is why MMU co-training is continued in stage 2, and the forecasts show that prediction learned from Bridge transfers to CALVIN scenes. Predicted futures show robot and object motion consistent with the instruction, but unseen scenes (D versus ABC) show background color artifacts.

